The M-curve is flat (Table~\ref{tab:smart_compress}): $M{=}16$ (56.9\%, 87.5\% compression) performs within 1.1pp of $M{=}128$ (58.0\%, no compression), and all five $M$ values cluster within 5pp. A parameter-matched MLP adapter (22.14M parameters) achieves 63.4\% $\pm$ 2.6 at $M{=}32$ ($p = 0.15$ vs.\ cross-attention), confirming re-encoding itself, not the attention mechanism, is the operative factor (Figure~\ref{fig:results_combined}b). Cross-suite evaluation confirms generalization: 53.2\% on LIBERO-Spatial and 56.4\% on LIBERO-Goal where hard pruning yields 0\% (Appendix~\ref{app:smart_compress_full}). Applying VTR to OpenVLA yields 0\% SR even in passthrough mode ($M{=}128$), indicating VTR is a targeted remedy for pixel-shuffle entanglement, not a universal compression module.

