\subsection{CV Predicts Optimal Pruning Strategy}
\label{sec:scaling_law}

The preceding sections establish that connector architecture determines pruning tolerance. A natural follow-up: can a single diagnostic predict not only \emph{how much} pruning a model tolerates, but also \emph{which} pruning strategy to use? Token importance CV provides exactly this dual prediction. Table~\ref{tab:scaling_law} compares L2 norm-based and random removal at $k{=}0.5$ across three models with measured CV.

\begin{table}[t]
